{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For with stammering speech.</b> Derived from the root לעג (Psalm 79:4), for so is the custom that the teacher speaks to the child." "<b>And in another tongue.</b> That the teacher should seek letters that are not harsh on the tongue in place of others; so it is fitting that the reprover speak to this people."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "Resolved אותו' as an abbreviation for אותיות based on the parallel in comment 1 where the teacher substitutes easier letters for harder ones; the abbreviation is unusual and the resolution uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:35.564635945Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}